*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.backup
.env.production
.env.staging
# Real env files are ignored above because Laravel loads .env.{APP_ENV} at boot, so those
# filenames mean "contains secrets". The .env.*.example templates are committed on
# purpose: they hold the non-secret half of each environment's config and are read by the
# deploy workflow. Keep that distinction, and never put a secret in a .example file.
